{'id': 'f0cb52f3-a4b3-5964-2160-96565bfc61e9', 'name': 'generate', 'error': None, 'result': [('generation', {'prefix': "The following code solves the N-Queens problem using backtracking. It places N queens on an N x N chessboard such that no two queens attack each other. The solution is visualized by printing the chessboard, where 'Q' represents a queen and '.' represents an empty space.", 'imports': '', 'code': 'def print_board(board):\n    n = len(board)\n    for row in board:\n        print(" ".join([\'Q\' if x else \'.\' for x in row]))\n    print("\\n")\n\ndef is_safe(board, row, col):\n    # Check this column on upper side\n    for i in range(row):\n        if board[i][col] == 1:\n            return False\n\n    # Check upper diagonal on left side\n    for i, j in zip(range(row, -1, -1), range(col, -1, -1)):\n        if board[i][j] == 1:\n            return False\n\n    # Check upper diagonal on right side\n    for i, j in zip(range(row, -1, -1), range(col, len(board))): \n        if board[i][j] == 1:\n            return False\n\n    return True\n\ndef solve_nqueens_util(board, row):\n    n = len(board)\n    if row >= n:\n        print_board(board)\n        return True\n\n    res = False\n    for col in range(n):\n        if is_safe(board, row, col):\n            board[row][col] = 1\n            res = solve_nqueens_util(board, row + 1) or res\n            board[row][col] = 0  # backtrack\n    return res\n\ndef solve_nqueens(n):\n    board = [[0] * n for _ in range(n)]\n    solve_nqueens_util(board, 0)\n\n# Example usage:\nsolve_nqueens(4)'}), ('messages', [AIMessage(content='The following code solves the N-Queens problem using backtracking. It places N queens on an N x N chessboard such that no two queens attack each other. The solution is visualized by printing the chessboard, where \'Q\' represents a queen and \'.\' represents an empty space. \n Imports:  \n Code: def print_board(board):\n    n = len(board)\n    for row in board:\n        print(" ".join([\'Q\' if x else \'.\' for x in row]))\n    print("\\n")\n\ndef is_safe(board, row, col):\n    # Check this column on upper side\n    for i in range(row):\n        if board[i][col] == 1:\n            return False\n\n    # Check upper diagonal on left side\n    for i, j in zip(range(row, -1, -1), range(col, -1, -1)):\n        if board[i][j] == 1:\n            return False\n\n    # Check upper diagonal on right side\n    for i, j in zip(range(row, -1, -1), range(col, len(board))): \n        if board[i][j] == 1:\n            return False\n\n    return True\n\ndef solve_nqueens_util(board, row):\n    n = len(board)\n    if row >= n:\n        print_board(board)\n        return True\n\n    res = False\n    for col in range(n):\n        if is_safe(board, row, col):\n            board[row][col] = 1\n            res = solve_nqueens_util(board, row + 1) or res\n            board[row][col] = 0  # backtrack\n    return res\n\ndef solve_nqueens(n):\n    board = [[0] * n for _ in range(n)]\n    solve_nqueens_util(board, 0)\n\n# Example usage:\nsolve_nqueens(4)', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={})]), ('iterations', 2)], 'interrupts': []}
